  "id": "COMPOUND:34325 - PROTEIN:6256",
  "verbalization": "Lupinisol A is shown to have a direct target relationship with CD276 antigen, which in turn is targeted by three different compounds—Merulinic Acid A, Pacificin F, and (2S,3R,3As,7Ar)-2-(1,3-Benzodioxol-5-Yl)-3A,7A-Dimethoxy-3-Methyl-5-Prop-2-Enyl-3,7-Dihydro-2H-1-Benzofuran-6-One—all of which ultimately target Histone H1.0. This suggests that Lupinisol A may exert its effects through a common mechanism, potentially inhibiting Histone H1.0, which plays a critical role in chromatin structure and gene regulation. The consistent targeting of CD276 antigen by multiple compounds and its subsequent targeting of Histone H1.0 indicates a plausible, mechanistically linked pathway. The evidence supports a potential role for Lupinisol A in modulating histone function, though further investigation is needed to confirm the specific mechanism of action and its relevance to disease.",
